# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
.astro/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/ is DELIBERATELY NOT ignored.
#
# A hook only binds behaviour if the settings file defining it is tracked in
# git. Quorum-AI's .gitignore:27 ignores `.claude/`, which silently demotes its
# four hooks — including the one blocking `--no-verify` — to local-only: they
# bind that machine and nobody else's.
#
# Per DAY-ONE-PROMPT.md: "to make a hook shared, deliberately un-ignore its
# settings file." So `.claude/settings.json` is tracked and carries the shared
# gates. Only the personal override below is ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# Impeccable working state — regenerated, machine-specific
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/config.local.json

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Visual walkthrough output — regenerate with node tests/visual-walkthrough.mjs
tests/shots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Brand candidates are NEVER tracked.
#
# Two reasons, both learned the hard way on 2026-08-07:
#
# 1. PRIVACY. The owner's visiting-card images contain a personal mobile
#    number and a LinkedIn QR, rendered as pixels. Every text-based secret
#    scanner missed them. They were swept in by `git add -A` and reached a
#    commit in a repo being prepared for publication. Caught before any push.
#
# 2. PROTOCOL. Claude must produce wordmark options WITHOUT seeing the
#    owner's, or the second opinion is just a reaction to the first.
#    Untracked files cannot be swept in by accident.
#
# The chosen mark gets added deliberately, as a single file, after review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/brand/candidates/rohit/*
!docs/brand/candidates/rohit/PUT-YOURS-HERE.txt
docs/brand/candidates/claude/*
!docs/brand/candidates/claude/.gitkeep

# Workflow worktrees — scratch, never committed
.claude/worktrees/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The WHOLE inbox is untracked. It is staging, not a site directory.
#
# Widened 2026-08-09, from brand-only to everything, after the owner uploaded
# his CV and a scan found a 10-digit phone number in
# FINAL-Rohit_Master_Resume.md. Those files were still untracked, so nothing
# reached a commit -- but under the previous rule photo/ and resume/ WERE
# tracked, and the next `git add -A` would have put a personal number into a
# repo being prepared to go public.
#
# This is the third time source material has carried personal contact details
# into this repo: visiting cards on 08-07, and now a CV.
#
# Files graduate from here into public/ or into page content DELIBERATELY,
# one at a time, after a human has looked at what is in them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/inbox/**
!assets/inbox/README.md
!assets/inbox/*/
!assets/inbox/*/.gitkeep

# Local wrangler state — miniflare caches and trace stores, machine-local
.wrangler/

# Throwaway comparison mockup — deleted once the visual world is chosen
mockup/
